<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">District of Branković</h1><p class="st-meta">1371 CE – 1412 CE (approx.) · capital Priština</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Lordship of Vuk Branković in Kosovo and northern Macedonia, rich in silver mines, which later merged into the Serbian Despotate.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vuk-brankovic">Vuk Branković</a>, son-in-law of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lazar-of-serbia">Prince Lazar</a>, built up lands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a> after the collapse of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbian-empire">Serbian Empire</a>. From about 1371 he held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pristina">Priština</a>, Peć and the mining districts, and later took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skopje">Skopje</a>, ruling as Lazar's ally.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vuk-brankovic">Vuk</a> ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pristina">Priština</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vucitrn">Vučitrn</a>, drawing income from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mines of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trepca">Trepča</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/novo-brdo">Novo Brdo</a> and protecting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbian-patriarchate-of-pec">Patriarchate of Peć</a>. He fought at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a> in 1389 and survived; later legend unjustly made him the traitor of the battle. Afterwards he resisted Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassalage</a> longer than other Serbian lords, seeking help from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vuk-brankovic">Vuk</a> and he died in captivity in 1397. His sons, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durad-brankovic">Đurađ Branković</a>, held part of his lands as Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> and in 1412 made peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-lazarevic">Stefan Lazarević</a>; the district merged into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbian-despotate">Serbian Despotate</a>, which Đurađ inherited in 1427.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/district-of-brankovic.jpg" alt="District of Branković" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_banner_of_Brankovi%C4%87_family.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1371 CE – 1412 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Priština</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Vuk Branković, Đurađ Branković</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Serbian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/kosovo">Kosovo</a>, <a href="/countries/serbia">Serbia</a>, <a href="/countries/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lands of Vuk Branković, Oblast Brankovića</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1392&amp;focus=district-of-brankovic" aria-label="District of Branković on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5192 661 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where District of Branković lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5512 917L5521 939M5512 917L5709 970M5512 917L5488 850"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5521 939h0M5709 970h0M5488 850h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5512 917h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5512 917h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Priština. <a href="/atlas?year=1392&amp;focus=district-of-brankovic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
